er three let's  talk about the anime goblin Slayer was  adapted by the animation studio white  fox this is a perfect fit  since the studio focuses on adapting  dark fantasy light novels and other  dramatic amateur content and goblins  slayer is definitely mature white fox  release entertaining and financially  successful anime like reezy row and  steins gate which is one of my favorite  anime of all time so let's just say that  as far as Studios go I have my hopes  high for this anime adaptation and I  think they've been doing a great job so  far  furthermore the director taka Haru Ozaki  also worked on our easy row and even  Cowboy Bebop albeit he wasn't the  director but still if you contributed to  Cowboy Bebop in any way that's gotta be  a good sign all things considered  there's reason to have faith in this  anime adaptation also if we can go by  the overlord formula which uses three  light novel volumes to create one  12-episode anime season  then we should almost have enough light  novel material for three 12-episode  anime seasons of goblin slayer  man that must be a lot of goblin slang  fact number four next we turn to kona  light novel GAO Sugoi translation this  light novel is amazing which is an  annual light novel guidebook which ranks  the top ten light novels of the year  according to readers pulled on the  internet this annual magazine is a  pretty big deal for light novel fans and  many of the light novels featured in it  were turned into anime like sword are  aligned kono Suba re0 and overlord to  name a few in 2017 goblin slayer got  fifth place in its category beating out  kono Suba which got ninth and scoring  just behind sword are online which came  in 4th place and it did all this without  anime height now with the anime finally  out I wouldn't be surprised that goblin  Slayer appeared on the top 10 list again  in 2019 perhaps even scoring higher than  5th place I guess we'll just have to  wait and see fact number 5 a big source  of kumo inspiration for Goblet Slayer  comes from classic fantasy novels rather  than being influenced by current works  Cuomo admits that he is more heavily  influenced by older fantasy stories  which is likely why his main character  unlike so many other main characters  today is actually from the fantasy world  and not just a modern-day person trapped  in a virtual fantasy game j.r.r tolkien  who wrote classics like The Hobbit and  The Lord of the Rings book series  appears to be one of kumo influences for  instance high elf Archer calls goblin  Serra orc bull when asked what it means  she explains and I quote it's the name  of a sword that appears in our legends  it was a goblin sling blade that would  glow blue when an orc a goblin was near  in the hobbit there's a similar blade  called or crest it was made by elven  Smith's and also glowed blue  when orcs or goblins were nearby another  name for it was goblin-cleaver  and the goblins called it biter both  blades had ork in their respective names  clawed blue and slayed goblins this is  just one example of how kuma pays homage  to Tolkien in his own fantasy novel fact  number six in my top 10 faction number  overlord video I let you guys know that  marui yama doesn't show his face  Mariama even went to anime expo wearing  a skeleton mask to hide his face even  though it was super hot  speaking of which Anime Expo 2018 was  also the first overseas convention that  cumo kagu went to it was also where  guests got a sneak preview of the Goblin  Slayer anime although I'm not sure if  kuhmo wore anything to cover his face at  the expo like midoriyama it is likely he  did since he usually does I could not  find his actual face on the Internet  but I did find him wearing what appears  to be a Deadpool mask a few times which  is pretty cool if you were at Anime Expo  and saw his panel definitely let us know  in the comments if you saw his actual  face or if not what kind of mask he had  fact number 7 along with classic fantasy  ku mole has admitted that he is a big  fan of tabletop RPGs like Dungeons &amp;  Dragons and that he was heavily  influenced by these types of games as  well he even tells people that if they  are also fans of these games he strongly  recommends that they check out goblin  Slayer the scenes in the light novel  where gods are rolling dice to decide  the fates of the characters in the world  of goblin slayer seems to hint at this  influence as well it is as if the story  is positioning the players of Dungeons &amp;  Dragons as gods and the world of goblin  Slayer is framed as if it was the game  that they are playing people have  noticed many similarities  for instance one goblin Slayer fan  pointed out that the adventure sheet  that priestess has to fill out is very  similar to a D&amp;D sheet if you have any  other clear references to D&amp;D and want  to share them feel free to put your  observations in the comments fact number  8 because this game is so heavily  influenced by tabletop or  PGs none of the characters have real  names rather they are named by their  class for instance goblin Slayers  childhood friend that he lives with is  simply called cowgirl while other  characters may simply be called warrior  or wizard because there are multiple  wizards in the world  you'll meet multiple characters named  wizard over the course of the story  let's just hope another goblin slayer  doesn't show up because then things may  start to get really confusing kuhmo  actually thought about giving the  characters proper names at one point but  ultimately decided against it in the  back of his mind he thought that all of  these characters were being played by  somebody on some tabletop RPG game so he  decided to let readers fill in the  blanks with their own names for the  characters let me know which character  you'd be if you could be anyone in  goblin slayer fact number 9 after this  fact the hitherto mentioned Deadpool  masks will suddenly start to make more  sense  Kumal has said along with being a fan of  Lord of the Rings and Dungeons and  Dragons he is also a big fan of American  comic books like my hero academia  creator Kohei horikoshi  and like horikoshi kuhmo was inspired by  the american comics he read in fact he  said that the motif of goblin slayer  came from american comics like Batman  The Punisher and more recently movies  like kick-ass instead of a kind of hero  who saves the world like Superman Goblin  flare is like this small-time hero that  isn't all that powerful who defeats the  local criminals and thugs he says he  wrote the story as if a Superman like  character exists already but on the side  there is the goblin Slayer doing his own  thing this is probably my favorite fact  and one of my favorite things about  goblin Slayer I absolutely love the fact  that he's not trying to be a Superman  and doesn't care what other people think  he's just doing what he feels is the  right thing to do doing the jobs that  those who are seeking glory and fame  won't fact number 10 you may well have  noticed that goblin Slayers armor is  pretty beat up and this includes his  helmet what you may not have known  that his helmet used to have horns like  that of a bull jutting out from each  side when goblin slayer was still a  greenhorn pun intended he lost them  the first horn was ripped off by a  goblin during his first goblin slaying  mission then instead of ripping the  other one off himself he does his goblin  slaying business for a while with one  horn then surprise surprise  another goblin rips off the other horn  then the goblin slayer losing all his  horns including his green one realizes  that maybe it's not a good idea having  horns for goblins to use as handlebars  and decides to go hornless from then on  and for a bonus fact you may not know  but on youtube you can also find a rare  interview with kuhmo on joeys aka the  anime man's channel he also starts off  that interview wearing his signature  Deadpool mask and ther